<section class="scenes-guide" id="scenes-guide" aria-labelledby="scenes-title">
  <header>
    <p>FOUR SOUNDS · ONE PREPARED RIG</p>
    <h2 id="scenes-title">Change the whole moment with one switch.</h2>
    <span>Scenes recall values inside the current preset without reloading its audio engine.</span>
  </header>

  <div class="scene-steps">
    <article><b>01</b><h3>Enter Scenes</h3><p>Hold FS1 + FS2 for 600 ms. The four screen plates now match the four footswitches.</p></article>
    <article><b>02</b><h3>Recall</h3><p>Press FS1–FS4. Instant scenes switch at the next audio boundary; timed scenes move for their saved Enter time.</p></article>
    <article><b>03</b><h3>Read the state</h3><p><strong>Live</strong> is the sound you hear. <strong>Editing</strong> is the scene whose stored values you are changing.</p></article>
    <article><b>04</b><h3>Return</h3><p>Hold FS1 + FS2 again to return to Presets. Tuner and Looper keep their existing priority gestures.</p></article>
  </div>

  <div class="scene-notes">
    <article>
      <h3>Build a scene</h3>
      <p>Enable Scenes from the preset editor, name all four sounds, choose an Enter time, and mark eligible controls as <strong>This scene</strong>. Shared controls remain common to the preset.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep delay and reverb natural</h3>
      <p><strong>Cut</strong> fades the effect contribution out. <strong>Let ring</strong> stops new wet input and lets the existing bounded tail decay.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Save and share safely</h3>
      <p>Save stores all four scenes together. To send one sound to older software, flatten that scene into an ordinary preset; Ardor folds in its trim and removes scene-only actions.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

